      "content": "*Heart of Darkness* presented in Joseph Conrad's novel does not offer a straightforward romanticized view of Africa; instead, it depicts the continent as a corrupted space ravaged by European imperialism and exploitation. While Africans are often marginalized or treated as passive instruments of colonization in the narrative, the text deeply critiques the blindness and moral failure of the European characters who densify a theme of civilizing progress as a facade for brutality. To frame your seminar discussion effectively, you should focus on how the story exposes the destructive nature of colonialism and questions the definitions of humanity and civilization within the post-colonial context.",
