      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a fair way to look at it for a seminar, but i'm also worried about the \"realism\" aspect. if the book is meant to show the corruption of the colonizers, then the racist language is technically a \"correct\" or \"accurate\" reflection of what people actually thought back then, right? like, if he had made the characters more progressive or used \"polite\" language, it wouldn't be a realistic depiction of the 19th century. so is there a point where we have to just accept the language as a neutral historical fact of the era?",
